          </div>
          <div class="related-card">
            <a href="/reviews/squarespace-vs-wix/">Squarespace vs Wix</a>
            <p>Templates vs drag-and-drop — which website builder is better for beginners?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="related-card">
            <a href="/reviews/best-website-builders-2026/">Best Website Builders 2026</a>
            <p>Our flagship ranked list of website builders for design, business, and developers.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="related-card">
            <a href="/reviews/website-builder/">Website Builder Pillar Hub</a>
            <p>Browse all website builder reviews, comparisons, and buying guides.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 id="buying-guide">How to Choose a WordPress Alternative in 2026</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Step 1 — Identify why you are leaving WordPress:</strong> Server maintenance → Webflow or Squarespace. Plugin conflicts → any hosted platform. Design limitations → Webflow or Framer. Ecommerce complexity → Shopify.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 2 — Test the free tier:</strong> Webflow, Wix, and Framer all have free tiers. Squarespace offers a 14-day trial. Build one real page before paying.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 3 — Evaluate design skill:</strong> Designer → Webflow or Framer. Non-designer → Squarespace or Wix. Developer → Webflow or headless approach.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 4 — Check SEO capabilities:</strong> All platforms in this list have adequate SEO. Webflow and Squarespace have the cleanest URL structures and meta controls.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 5 — Plan migration:</strong> Most platforms import WordPress XML. Images and text transfer cleanly; plugin-specific data may require manual migration. Set up 301 redirects for every URL change.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Learn more about our <a href="/how-we-test/">testing methodology</a> and <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>What is the best alternative to WordPress in 2026?</summary>
          <p>Webflow is the best overall alternative to WordPress in 2026 for designers and developers who want visual design control without server maintenance. Squarespace is the best for non-technical users who want beautiful templates. Shopify is the best for ecommerce. The right choice depends on your primary use case: content site, portfolio, ecommerce, or web app.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is Webflow better than WordPress?</summary>
          <p>Webflow is better than WordPress for designers who want pixel-perfect visual control without writing PHP or managing servers. WordPress is better for content-heavy sites, blogs, and teams that need the 60,000+ plugin ecosystem. Webflow's hosting, CMS, and visual editor are more modern; WordPress offers more flexibility and lower cost. See our WordPress vs Webflow comparison for the full breakdown.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What is the cheapest WordPress alternative?</summary>
          <p>Wix is the cheapest WordPress alternative for beginners, with the Business Basic plan at $17/month including hosting, SSL, and a drag-and-drop builder. Squarespace Personal at $16/month is comparable. For ecommerce, Shopify Starter at $39/month is the most value-complete option. WordPress itself is free, but hosting ($5–$25/month) plus premium plugins ($50–$200/year) often costs more than a hosted alternative.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I migrate from WordPress to another platform?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Most platforms offer WordPress import tools. Webflow, Squarespace, Wix, and Shopify all support content migration from WordPress XML exports. Images and text transfer cleanly; custom post types and plugin-specific data may require manual migration. The biggest challenge is preserving SEO — plan 301 redirects for every URL that changes to maintain search rankings.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

